    {
      "id": "economics",
      "beats": [
        {
          "beat": 1,
          "vo_text": "I put the exact scoring rubric, the demo-first outreach sequence, and the full tool stack from this pipeline into a blueprint \u2014 link's below if you want the working version instead of rebuilding it from scratch.",
          "highlight_words": [
            "blueprint",
            "working version"
          ],
          "asset_hint": "slide: blueprint mockup cover",
          "source": null
        },
        {
          "beat": 2,
          "vo_text": "Realistic range for a side operation, a handful of clients at fifteen to twenty hours a week, is somewhere in the two to five thousand a month territory \u2014 that's a floor built from the low end of the solo pricing band, not a promise.",
          "highlight_words": [
            "two to five thousand",
            "not a promise"
          ],
          "asset_hint": "chart: effort level (hrs/week) vs revenue range, three tiers",
          "source": "Brainy Papers pricing band; estimate based on partial capacity"
        },
        {
          "beat": 3,
          "vo_text": "Full-time at Designjoy's reported shape \u2014 thirty-five clients, five thousand a month each \u2014 the self-reported range runs from one to three million a year. That figure has no audit behind it, and this episode isn't asking you to trust it, just to know it's the only public data point at this scale.",
          "highlight_words": [
            "one to three million",
            "no audit"
          ],
          "asset_hint": "slide: 'Full-time, self-reported: $1M-$3M/yr. Unaudited.'",
          "source": "Aggregated Designjoy sources [reported \u26a0\ufe0f]"
        },
        {
          "beat": 4,
          "vo_text": "What this actually diversifies is skill, not just income: client acquisition, pricing, and AI-tool fluency that transfer to any service business. The real risk isn't the work \u2014 it's retention. Lose three of thirty-five clients on flat pricing and that's fifteen thousand dollars gone in a month.",
          "highlight_words": [
            "skill, not just income",
            "fifteen thousand dollars gone"
          ],
          "asset_hint": "slide: 'Churn math: -3 clients = -$15,000/mo'",
          "source": "Estimate from Designjoy's reported client count and price point"
        },
        {
          "beat": 5,
          "vo_text": "And the harder failure mode is distribution, not delivery. The pricing page is copyable in an afternoon. Designjoy's own stated growth engine was roughly six million tweet impressions built over years \u2014 the part almost nobody selling this playbook mentions.",
          "highlight_words": [
            "copyable in an afternoon",
            "six million tweet impressions"
